  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1222 AM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nSaturday through Wednesday:\n\nTemperatures will quickly recover on Saturday as the low exits\nand strong high pressure sets up over the Midwest. Yet another\nsurface trough developing in the Northern Plains will keep our\npressure gradient tight over WI on Sat, so expect breezy\nsouthwest winds (but only to around 20 mph) and highs recovering\ninto the mid to upper 50s. Breezy southwest winds will continue\nSunday and highs should manage to reach 60. \n\nThe warm-up will continue through Thursday as we largely remain\nin southerly flow. Highs will be in the 60s, but get up to \naround 70 by later in the week. \n\nThe weather will remain largely dry from Saturday through\nThursday. There is one weak shortwave that cold bring a period\nof clouds and a few sprinkles on Monday. \n\nCronce",
